sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor Worker as Channel Delivery Worker
    participant Breaker as Circuit Breaker (MSG91)
    participant Primary as Primary Provider (MSG91)
    participant Secondary as Failover Provider (Twilio)
    participant WA as Fallback Channel (WhatsApp)
    participant Ops as Operations Alerting & Sentry
    participant StateMachine as State Machine & State Log

    Note over Breaker: State = CLOSED (Healthy)
    Worker->>Breaker: canExecute()?
    Breaker-->>Worker: true
    Worker->>Primary: send(notification)
    Primary-->>Worker: HTTP 503 / Gateway Timeout (Failure 1)
    Worker->>Breaker: recordFailure()
    
    loop 4 additional failures within 60s
        Worker->>Primary: send(notification)
        Primary-->>Worker: Gateway Timeout
        Worker->>Breaker: recordFailure()
    end
    
    Note over Breaker: 5 Failures Reached ➔ State = OPEN
    Breaker->>Ops: Emit Alert: "MSG91 Breaker OPEN - High Error Rate"
    
    Worker->>Breaker: canExecute()?
    Breaker-->>Worker: false (Bypass Primary)
    Worker->>Secondary: Dispatch via Twilio Failover
    Secondary-->>Worker: HTTP 201 Created (Success)
    Worker->>StateMachine: Transition to SENT (Provider: Twilio, fallbackUsed: true)
    
    alt If both SMS providers fail (Non-critical notification)
        Worker->>WA: Reroute to WhatsApp Cloud API
        WA-->>Worker: HTTP 200 Delivered
    end

    Note over Breaker: After 60s Cooldown Window
    Note over Breaker: State = HALF_OPEN (Testing recovery)
    Worker->>Primary: Probe Canary Request
    alt Probe Succeeds
        Breaker->>Breaker: State = CLOSED (Recovered)
        Breaker->>Ops: Emit Alert: "MSG91 Recovered to CLOSED"
    else Probe Fails
        Breaker->>Breaker: State = OPEN (Cooldown resets for 60s)
    end
